  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Limited ed. of 100 copies signed and numbered by the author; some include a signed and numbered lithograph in an envelope attached to the back cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Spiral bound; front and back covers are color illustrated and laminated. Satirical children's coloring and activity book format of cartoon outline drawings of children engaged in various dissolute activities, interspersed with historical references.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="501" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">With: single "A Winning Team" lithograph which has been hand printed and signed by the author. UCSD's copy of lithograph is numbered 11/36.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">CU-S</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"An unlikely character for a coloring book, Jean Genet has never looked more friendly and approachable than he does in Let's Play!. Drawn in the simplified cartoon style of so many 'educational' books for children, the robberies, prison stints, gambling tables, beggars, lice, and tatoos pictured on these pages teach children about a world beyond the reach of their scribbling scrabbling crayons."--Printed Matter, Inc. website, viewed May 20, 2013.</subfield>
  </datafield>
